{"type": "say", "text": "Good morning everyone. I wanted to get us together to discuss the eight drums of spent solvent from the coatings area that are staged for disposition. As you know, they haven't been released for shipment yet, and our approved waste contractor is available to receive them during the current workweek. Before I can sign the final shipment authorization and paperwork, our company procedure requires a pre-shipment review with laboratory, waste logistics, maintenance, and production. So I'd like to use this time to conduct that review and make sure we have everything in order. Who would like to start?"}
```

```json
{"type": "reveal", "fact_id": "PF1", "text": "I can start on the laboratory side. I tested a representative sample from those drums yesterday and recorded a 54°C flash point. Because of that result, the current waste profile requires the shipment to be documented as waste code D001 and transported as UN1993, flammable liquid, n.o.s., Packing Group III. I completed the lab worksheet, but I want to flag that it has not yet been attached to the waste file, so we need to make sure that gets done before shipment."}
```

```json
{"type": "say", "text": "Thanks, Leon. On the waste logistics side, I can confirm that our approved contractor is ready to receive the drums. I have a specific pickup window confirmed with them, but let me share that detail formally so it's on the record for everyone."}
```

```json
{"type": "reveal", "fact_id": "PF3", "text": "On the maintenance side, I need to flag something from my inspection of the staged drums. Drums 3 and 6 have damaged bung threads. Each of those two drums must be placed in a UN-rated overpack before loading. I noted the finding on my inspection sheet, but I want everyone to be aware that the maintenance system has not been updated yet, so it won't show up there if anyone is checking electronically."}
```

```json
{"type": "reveal", "fact_id": "PF4", "text": "On the production side, I need to flag something important. My batch records show that drums 7 and 8 contain residual isocyanate catalyst from a separate coating formulation. Our production handling instruction requires those two drums to travel on a separate pallet with a catalyst-residue notation. I want everyone to be aware that I have retained the batch records for the shift closeout and have not yet sent them to compliance, so they won't be in the compliance file yet."}
```

